  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Given that $X∼\\text{Bernoulli}(\\frac{1}{3}),$ compute $P(X=0).$",
  "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Bernoulli}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function: \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}p, & x=1 \\\\ 1-p, & x=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Bernoulli}(\\frac{1}{3}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=0)=f(0)=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$",
